window.CLUBS = [{"id":"404071","key":"101stem","name":"101 STEM Consulting","shortName":null,"summary":"101 STEM Consulting is a student-led organization that bridges the gap between STEM and business through innovative consulting solutions.","description":"101 STEM Consulting is a student-led organization at Indiana University Bloomington that bridges the gap between STEM and business through hands-on consulting experiences. We collaborate with nonprofits and local organizations to deliver impactful insights, foster creative problem-solving, and drive data-driven strategies that support STEM education and community initiatives.\n\nOur members come from a variety of academic backgrounds, including science, technology, business, and education, and work together to tackle real-world challenges. Whether it’s helping a company improve STEM programming or supporting a nonprofit with data analysis and strategic planning, we empower our consultants to turn ideas into actionable solutions. Along the way, students gain valuable experience in client collaboration, project management, and interdisciplinary thinking.\n\nWhether you\u0027re a STEM enthusiast looking to explore business applications or a business student eager to dive into the world of technology, 101 STEM Consulting provides a platform to grow, learn, and make a difference. Join us as we shape the future of STEM consulting one project at a time.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Z - Works with Children","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"132675","key":"180dc","name":"180 Degrees Consulting","shortName":"180 DC","summary":"180 Degrees Consulting is a student-run consultancy focused on serving nonprofits and social enterprises.","description":"180 Degrees Consulting provides socially conscious organizations around the world with high-quality consulting services. We work with organizations to develop innovative, practical, and sustainable solutions to whatever challenges they’re facing.\n\n180 Degrees Consulting connects the untapped capabilities of top undergraduate students with the unmet needs of socially conscious organizations. Importantly, the process is mutually beneficial. Non-profits, social enterprises, and socially-minded businesses get custom solutions to problems they’re facing and our students get work experience, professional training, first-hand exposure to non-profits and social enterprises, real leadership development, and the opportunity to make a difference.\n\nFollow our Website and Instagram to stay updated on our organization and our recruitment process!\n\nInstagram: @180dcindiana\n\nWebsite:  www.180dcindiana.com","categories":["Academic and Professional","Environmental and Sustainability","Service and Philanthropy","Z - New Member Training","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"335409","key":"812consulting","name":"812 Consulting","shortName":null,"summary":"We work with clients to solve their toughest challenges today while developing their leaders of tomorrow. We proudly partner with clients who accelerate the growth and development of our members.","description":"At 812 Consulting, we place students on client-facing engagements with real-world businesses while fostering a culture of mentorship and friendship. Our goal is to uplift one another and grow—both professionally and personally—as a community.\n\nOur mission is rooted in our members. We aim to build the best environment for learning and development for the brightest, most passionate students at Indiana University. While \"consulting\" is in our name, we are not just a pre-professional club focused\r\n on consulting careers. Our mission is your growth—wherever that path may lead.\n\n812 Consulting is an application-based organization. We accept new members each semester based on available spots for client projects. Please follow us on LinkedIn and Instagram to stay up to date.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"342251","key":"actuarialclub","name":"Actuarial Club at Indiana University","shortName":"Actuarial Club","summary":"The Actuarial Club connects students with an interest in actuarial science. The club provides networking opportunities with professionals and gives students the resources needed to take and pass actuarial exams.","description":"The Actuarial Club at Indiana University seeks to do the following:\n- Connect prospective actuaries with exam resources and other knowledgeable students for professional growth and development\n- Provide networking opportunities with professionals currently in the field, developing relationships and educating about the actuarial career path\n- Allow students the opportunity to practice their actuarial skills in the annual SOA Case Study Challenge\n\nActuaries work at the intersection of mathematics, data science, and business to assess risk and uncertainty. They seek to determine the financial impact of possible future events. You could find a career as an actuary fulfilling if you:\n- Are a quantitative thinker that loves to solve problems, willing to embark on the examination process to become a credentialed actuary\n- Want to maintain work-life balance while being compensated well, as the median actuary works 40 hours per week and makes $108,000 per year\n- Are looking for a stable career where demand is growing, as actuarial jobs are expected to grow by 18% over the next 10 years and the insurance industry is highly resilient to recessions\n\nJoin our GroupMe: https://groupme.com/join_group/71929245/qBqT4VWX","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133536","key":"akpsi","name":"Alpha Kappa Psi - Beta Gamma Chapter","shortName":"AKPsi","summary":"A co-ed professional business fraternity that combines professional and personal growth of its members.","description":"*Recruitment for Alpha Kappa Psi will begin at the beginning of each semester. Look at our website \u0026 Instagram for application info and deadlines (@akpsi_iu)\n\nAlpha Kappa Psi is America\u0027s first professional business fraternity. Founded October 5, 1904 at New York University, AKPsi now has more than 230 college and alumni chapters. The objects of Alpha Kappa Psi are: 1) To further the individual welfare of its members, 2) To foster scientific research in the fields of commerce, accounts, and finance, 3) To educate the public to appreciate and demand higher ideals therein, and 4) To promote and advance in institutions of college rank, courses leading to degrees in business administration. Members of our chapter equally value the ideals of brotherhood, professionalism, and community service.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","Service and Philanthropy","Z - Travel","Z - Works with Children","Z - New Member Training","Z - Travel - Service","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133689","key":"abp","name":"Alternative Break Program","shortName":"ABP","summary":"Developing global leaders during service-learning trips over Thanksgiving, Winter and Spring breaks. A proud Kelley Institute for Social Impact (KISI) partner. Applications for 2026-2027 open on August 31st, 2026.","description":"Participant Applications open on August 31st, 2026!\n\nThrough international and domestic service-learning trips, ABP gives students the opportunity to not only learn about social issues and connect with like-minded peers, but also allows them to see how their service can leave a lasting impression in communities around the world.\n\nAs a participant, you will travel to a community in a team of 5 to 12, engage in active service, and have the opportunity to gain new perspectives on social issues.\n\nAs a Site Leader, you would work with our executive team to help plan and organize a trip and take charge while on the trip. Participants will have the opportunity to travel, learn, and engage in service work alongside site leaders. We only have a few site leader spots available at this time; however, if you are interested in being a site leader, I encourage you to fill out the site leader application.\n\nCheckout our Instagram @abp.at.iub or our website https://iuabp.org/ for more details!\n\nPlease feel free to reach out with any questions to abp@iu.edu or vameye@iu.edu","categories":["Environmental and Sustainability","International and Multicultural","Service and Philanthropy","Z - Travel","Z - Travel - International","Z - Works with Children","IU Kelley School of Business","Alternative Break Experiences","Career Community - Education, Non-Profit, + Social Services","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"352469","key":"aig","name":"Alternative Investment Group","shortName":"AIG","summary":"The Alternative Investment Group is a student-led club focused on exploring non-traditional investments such as private equity, real estate, hedge funds, and derivatives—going beyond cash, bonds, and stocks to deepen financial understanding.","description":"The Alternative Investment Group is a student-led organization dedicated to learning about non-traditional investment strategies and asset classes. Our focus goes beyond cash, bonds, and stocks to explore areas like private equity, hedge funds, real estate, and commodities. We’ll also dive into different forms of trading to better understand how these markets work. Whether you\u0027re curious about the broader world of finance or interested in expanding your knowledge, this club offers a unique space to explore alternative investments in a collaborative environment.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133216","key":"ama_iu","name":"American Marketing Association at Indiana University","shortName":"AMA","summary":"The American Marketing Association at Indiana University is an all-encompassing marketing organization,\r\ndevoted to educating and empowering members through hands-on experience and professional development to prepare them for their future career.","description":"The American Marketing Association at Indiana University is the all-encompassing marketing organization devoted to educating and empowering members through hands-on experience. We provide exclusive professional development for our members spanning experiential events, networking opportunities, and educational moments to prepare them for their future careers.\n\nInterested in joining? Head over to our official website or Instagram account for the most up-to-date information about involvement and what we do.\n\n@ama.iu\n\nWebsite","categories":["Academic and Professional","Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Marketing, Advertising, + Public Relations","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"405271","key":"ap","name":"Aperture Partners","shortName":"AP","summary":"AP hopes to provide IU\u0027s students an opportunity to explore the interdisciplinary fields of Finance, Strategy, Tech and Marketing through our client\u0027s projects!","description":"Aperture Partners (AP) is a student-led 501(c)(3) organization at Indiana University that provides consulting, tech, finance, and marketing solutions to real-world clients. We empower members with hands-on experience, mentorship, and leadership opportunities\r\n to grow into impactful, future-ready professionals.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133494","key":"ascendiub","name":"Ascend at Indiana University","shortName":"Ascend","summary":"Ascend at Indiana University is a leadership focused business organization composed of, but not limited, to Pan-Asians. Students with any majors are welcomed to join. Please subscribe to our newsletter to receive more information!","description":"Ascend at Indiana University Bloomington is one of the student chapters of Ascend National, which is a premier professional organization nationwide dedicated to enabling its members, business partners, and the community to leverage the leadership and global business potential of Pan-Asians. It is a lifelong organization supporting the duration of our members\u0027 careers from undergraduate through to executive level. Membership is open to individuals of all ethnic and professional backgrounds, ages, and geographic locations.\n\nThe vision of Ascend is to enhance the presence and influence of current and future business leaders of Asian and Pacific Islander descent and to serve as a collective voice for those business communities. Our national and regional chapter programs help us:\n\n· Cultivate the leadership development and professional growth of members\n\n· Build eminence and visibility for Asians and to provide role models\n\n· Provide business growth opportunities for our members and corporate partners\n\n· Encourage the continuous presence and influence of Asians in the global economy\n\n· Bridge the Cultural Difference gap between Asian and Western cultures\n\n· Serve the public interest in the community and provide thought leadership","categories":["Academic and Professional","International and Multicultural","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"383451","key":"assetmanagementclub","name":"Asset Management Club at IU","shortName":"AMC","summary":"An undergraduate student organization focused on helping underclassmen through an extensive financial services bootcamp","description":"The Asset Management Club at Indiana University is centered around growing the personal and technical skills of financial prospects. Our program is designed to build both professionalism and technical skill through a structured, semester-long experience. Applications open every spring.\n\nMembers begin with several weeks focused on professional development—covering LinkedIn, Resumes, Cover Letters, Behavioral Interview Skills, and foundational market knowledge—before rotating through each of our specialized tracks, including Investment Banking, Research, Private Wealth Management, Sales \u0026 Trading, Commercial Real Estate, and Wealth Management. These rotations give students hands-on exposure to the core functions, analytical tools, and day-to-day responsibilities of each discipline, helping them identify where their interests and strengths align.\n\nAt the end of the semester, students participate in a selective interview process to earn placement into one of our track cohorts. These cohorts provide ongoing mentorship, technical training, and recruiting support throughout the workshop and internship process.\n\nAMC’s mission is to create a pipeline of well-prepared, market-literate, and professionally polished students who are ready to excel in high-finance careers. Through rigorous training, real-world exercises, and a strong community of mentors and alumni, we equip our members with the skills, confidence, and network needed to thrive in competitive markets-focused roles.\n\n2025-2026 Application: https://forms.gle/FdNzGK7JWF8p5sv57\n\nWebsite Link: https://www.assetmanagementclubiu.com/","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"166897","key":"aba","name":"Association for Business Analytics","shortName":"ABA","summary":"The Association for Business Analytics is a Kelley Student Organization dedicated to exploring career applications of analytics through corporate visits, professional development, and the creation of a strong student network.","description":"The Association for Business Analytics is a group of students committed to collaborating with each other to explore how the critical thinking skills they have learned in their courses can serve them in any future position. The goal of the ABA is to build a supportive network between students and develop strong critical thinking and business analytics skills through corporate visits, networking events, professional development workshops, and case competitions. The club also seeks to foster networking and peer mentoring relationships between members. The Association of Business Analytics aims to provide undergraduate students with the skills and knowledge they need to excel in any future endeavors through corporate visits, workshops, technical skill demonstrations, professor visits, case competitions, and networking opportunities. \n\nInterested in joining? Follow our Instagram (aba.iub) to be the first to hear about our Fall 2026 recruitment cycle.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"132678","key":"alpfaiub","name":"Association of Latino Professionals For America at IU","shortName":"ALPFA","summary":"We promote the principles of academic success, professional discipline, and personal development all while creating networking opportunities for members.","description":"ALPFA is a student chapter of the national professional Hispanic business organization which is dedicated to furthering the careers of today\u0027s Latino business professionals. We promote the principles of academic success, professional discipline, and personal development all while creating networking opportunities for members. Any individual is welcome to join ALPFA!","categories":["Academic and Professional","International and Multicultural","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"167546","key":"balance","name":"Balance at Kelley","shortName":"BAK","summary":"Balance at Kelley is an organization dedicated to reducing the stigma surrounding mental health through raising awareness, supplementing education, providing campus-wide resources, and starting the conversation.","description":"Involvement is open to ALL! Today is a great day to join! Attend one of our meetings or email tmcleary@iu.edu to join or get more information.\n\nBalance at Kelley is an organization dedicated to reducing the stigma surrounding mental health through raising awareness, creating community, supplementing education, providing campus-wide resources, and simply starting the conversation.\n\nWe hope to shed light on the presence of anxiety, depression, stress, imposter syndrome, and other mental health \u0026 wellness concerns within the Kelley School of Business and at IU. We accomplish this through events, social media, and collaboration with other\r\n organizations on campus.\n\nOur members will have the opportunity to engage with other students in a stigma-free environment where mental health can be openly discussed and free from judgement. Members will also have the opportunity to suggest and/or spearhead their own initiatives\r\n given the collaborative and supportive assistance of BAK members and leaders within KSB.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Healthcare + Wellness","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"324645","key":"bankingandtradingassociation","name":"Banking and Trading Association","shortName":"BTA","summary":"The Banking \u0026 Trading Association is dedicated to developing skills for students pursuing careers Investment Banking, Sales and Trading, and Equity Research.","description":"The Banking \u0026 Trading Association is dedicated to developing the technical, market-based, and professional skill sets required for students pursuing careers in Investment Banking, Sales \u0026 Trading, and Equity Research.\n\nThe organization provides a structured, hands-on learning environment through weekly meetings focused on financial modeling, valuation, and market analysis, alongside current events discussions. Members benefit from a mentorship program that connects underclassmen with experienced students who have successfully navigated recruiting processes.\n\nThe association plays a central role in preparing students for highly selective programs such as the Investment Banking Workshop (IBW) and Investment Management Workshop (IMW), offering targeted guidance on technical interviews, networking strategy, and behavioral preparation. It also hosts guest speakers from industry professionals, providing direct insight into career paths and day-to-day responsibilities.\n\nThrough these initiatives, the organization has consistently placed dozens of students each year into top-tier finance roles and the IU workshops, establishing a strong pipeline to careers on Wall Street.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"404075","key":"bsg","name":"Behavioral Strategy Group","shortName":"BSG","summary":"Behavioral Strategy Group (BSG) bridges behavioral economics and real-world impact, consulting for international governments, Fortune 500s, and startups. Join our weekly open meetings to explore how insights become action.","description":"Building on four years of success at Harvard College and a proven track record of working alongside international governments, Fortune 500 companies, and ambitious startups, Behavioral Strategy Group is excited to open its second domestic chapter at Indiana University. BSG is a collection of some of the brightest and most dedicated students around the globe applying academic insights to make progress on real world problems by consulting innovative and impactful organizations. At IU, BSG will continue its mission by providing science-backed consulting services and hosting weekly open-to-all meetings. These events will feature fireside chats with field leaders and in-depth workshops exploring the intersections of economics, psychology, policy, and business.\n\nAll links: https://linktr.ee/bsgiu\n\nEmail: board.bsg.iu@gmail.com","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133303","key":"iubap","name":"Beta Alpha Psi Honorary Accounting Organization","shortName":"BAP","summary":"BETA ALPHA PSI is an honorary accounting organization for financial information students and professionals. The primary objective of Beta Alpha Psi is to encourage and give recognition to professional excellence in the business information field","description":"BETA ALPHA PSI is an honorary Organization for financial information students and professionals. The primary objective of Beta Alpha Psi is to encourage and give recognition to scholastic and professional excellence in the business information field. This includes promoting the study and practice of accounting, finance, information systems, business analytics, and digital technology; providing opportunities for self-development, service and association among members and practicing professionals, and encouraging a sense of ethical, social, and public responsibility.\n\nThe purpose of Beta Alpha Psi is to:\n- Recognize outstanding academic achievements in the field of accounting, finance, information systems, business analytics, and digital technology;\n- Promote the study and practice of professional fields related to these disciplines;\n- Provide opportunities for self-development and association among members and practicing financial professionals;\n- encourage a sense of ethical, social, and public responsibilities.\n\nMISSION\n\nThe mission of Beta Alpha Psi, the premier international honor and service organization for financial and business information students and professionals, is to inspire and support excellence by:\n- Encouraging the study and practice of accountancy, finance, information systems, business analytics, and digital technology;\n- Providing opportunities for service, professional development, and interaction among members and financial professionals\n- Fostering lifelong ethical, social, and public responsibilities.\n\nFA26 – Recruitment\n\nCallout signups, applications, and club communication will be available through our Linktree. https://linktr.ee/BAPIUB","categories":["Academic and Professional","Honorary","Z - Travel","Z - New Member Training","Z - Travel - Service","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"375944","key":"binaryheart","name":"BinaryHeart at Indiana University","shortName":"BHIU","summary":"BinaryHeart is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit that donates computers. We collect devices (often donated to us), wipe their data, repair and update them, and donate them to underserved communities that lack digital access. Learn more at www.binaryheart.org/iu/join","description":"By distributing devices and teaching users best practices, we help communities access vital digital services, including telehealth, education, jobs, and more. BinaryHeart at Indiana University serves as a chapter of the larger BinaryHeart Indiana Inc. 501(c)(3)\r\n nonprofit, and collaborates with other chapters to spearhead efforts in bridging the digital divide.\n\nJoin us to make an impact, both in Bloomington and across the country. Here\u0027s how it works:\n\n1) We Collect Device Donations \u0026 Raise Funding\n\n2) We Diagnose, Wipe, \u0026 Refurbish Devices\n\n3) We Donate Devices to People in Need\n\nGiven the nature of our operations, we welcome students from (or interested in) all backgrounds, including but not limited to supply chain operations, process improvement, data analytics, computer engineering/science, marketing and media, finance, and technology.\n\nTo learn more, visit www.binaryheart.org/iu/join","categories":["Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"393066","key":"blackinbusiness","name":"Black in Business","shortName":"(BiB)","summary":"Brilliance. Developing. Impact. A professional community empowering Black business students to lead with brilliance, grow through development, and create lasting impact through mentorship, career preparation, academic support, and leadership development.","description":"Our organization aims to create a place for Black students at Indiana University, offering support through job preparation, networking, and mentoring services.\n\nOur mission is to foster a supportive community that empowers Black business students to achieve high academic performance, develop leadership skills, and seize professional growth opportunities. We are dedicated to:\n- Academic Excellence:\n- Encouraging high academic performance through study groups, tutoring services, and resource sharing.\n- Leadership Development:\n- Providing leadership opportunities within the organization, such as executive roles and committee positions, to help members build and demonstrate their leadership skills.\n- Professional Opportunities:\n- Facilitating open networking events, career nights, and hosting public speakers from various industries to expose members to potential career paths and professional growth.\n- Personal Growth:\n- Offering workshops on networking, interpersonal relationship development, and public speaking to enhance personal skills critical for success in business.\n- Regular Meetings and Events:\n- Conducting weekly meetings that include speeches on topics chosen by individual members, industry overviews, and presentations by company speakers.\n- Hosting workshops on writing, PowerPoint presentations, resume and cover letter preparation, and mock case competitions.\n- Providing mentoring services through a big-little program, ensuring every member has access to guidance and support from more experienced peers.\n- Current Events and Campus Resources:\n- Discussing weekly current events in the business world with a focus on issues relevant to Black students.\n- Providing a campus resources guide and statistics on the experiences of Black people on campus and in the workplace.\n- Community Engagement:\n- Organizing volunteer opportunities to give back to the community and foster a spirit of service among members.\n\nThrough these initiatives, Black in Business seeks to not only support its members academically and professionally but also to build a strong network of Black business professionals who are well-prepared to navigate and succeed in the business world.","categories":["Academic and Professional","International and Multicultural","Social","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"181861","key":"iubcc","name":"Blockchain@IU","shortName":"BCCIU","summary":"Blockchain@IU is an innovative student-run organization committed to advancing the research, development, and education of blockchain technology.","description":"Blockchain@IU is an innovative student-run organization that is committed to advancing the research, development, and education of blockchain technology.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133506","key":"beppclub","name":"Business Economics and Public Policy Club","shortName":"BEPP Club","summary":"Bridging the worlds of business, economics, and policy while fostering connections with industry leaders and academic mentors, empowering members to engage in impactful research and consultancy endeavors.","description":"Welcome to the Business Economics and Public Policy Club! As a specialized departmental organization, we are committed to fostering the growth of our members through skill development in networking, not only with diverse companies but also by building relationships with esteemed professors within our department. Our primary focus revolves around nurturing core consultancy abilities, empowering individuals to analyse, strategise, and excel in the realms of business economics and public policy. Through a variety of events and engaging case competitions, we provide a dynamic platform where members can hone their expertise, exchange innovative ideas, and actively contribute to shaping the future of these intersecting fields. Join us to explore a realm of professional growth, collaborative learning, and impactful networking opportunities! \n\nJoin our club below!\n\nGroupMe: https://groupme.com/join_group/117008124/oFsjLl86","categories":["Academic and Professional","International and Multicultural","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"405776","key":"bcc","name":"Business in Cosmetics Club at Indiana University","shortName":"BCC","summary":"BCC is a professional development and philanthropic organization, with the mission to develop beauty enthusiasts into the future leaders of corporate beauty.","description":"The Business in Cosmetics Club at Indiana University is a professional development and philanthropic organization for beauty enthusiasts passionate about the intersection of business and cosmetics (including makeup, skincare,\r\n haircare, and fragrance). Our mission is to develop, educate, and empower the next generation of leaders in the corporate beauty industry, while fostering a commitment in giving back to the community. Through keystone events\r\n like guest speaker panels, brand partnerships, and fundraisers, we create opportunities for growth, connection, and impact.\n\nInstagram: bcc.inbloom","categories":["Academic and Professional","Arts and Entertainment","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"193818","key":"bli","name":"Business Leadership Initiative at IU Hillel","shortName":"BLI","summary":"In partnership with IU Hillel, BLI gives business students an opportunity to learn from accomplished Jewish executives. Participants are able to meet with these professionals in a relaxed, small group setting and engage with them in open dialogue.","description":"Applications for Spring of 2026 will open soon!\n\nBLI is an exclusive, unique opportunity for exceptional business students to learn from and network with some of the leading Jewish business executives in the country. Within the framework of a small group you will be able to\r\n meet with these executives in a relaxed setting and engage with them in open dialogue. These professionals, who have generously given their time, are eager to get to know you and speak with you about how they achieved their success.\n\nIn addition to gaining a network of peers and professionals, BLI offers professional growth opportunities, including resume and LinkedIn workshops, and BLI Connect, a mentorship program exclusively for BLI members.","categories":["Religious and Spiritual","Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"350034","key":"businessworldofentertainment","name":"Business World of Entertainment","shortName":"BWE","summary":"This organization aims to look at the Business side of Hollywood and entertainment. With box office breakdowns, news discussions, industry guest speakers, informational workshops, and more!","description":"We are a club that explores various topics surrounding the entertainment industry. We hold educational meetings to build an understanding of different industries within entertainment, as well as invite speakers to share their experiences and build relationships with members. We meet every other Wednesday. Check out our Instagram and GroupMe to stay updated on meetings!\n\nInstagram: @BWE_iu\n\nGroupMe: https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgroupme.com%2Fjoin_group%2F84785349%2FUhbI0t3w\u0026data=05%7C02%7Ckayfren%40iu.edu%7C001a7ae04df447574b3308de94b7a707%7C1113be34aed14d00ab4bcdd02510be91%7C1%7C0%7C639111713655732808%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C\u0026sdata=YKc%2BBceyyzoflvzQWLluEoadsdCQI3H7szj6RYrZEQY%3D\u0026reserved=0","categories":["Academic and Professional","Arts and Entertainment","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"347884","key":"capitalmarketsclub","name":"Capital Markets Club","shortName":"CMC","summary":"Learn more and apply at https://cmciu.com.\n\nPrepares students for careers in investment banking, private equity, equity research, sales \u0026 trading, and private wealth management through technical education, mentorship, networking, and hands-on","description":"Capital Markets Club (CMC) is one of Indiana University\u0027s premier undergraduate finance organization dedicated to preparing students for careers across the capital markets industry.\n\nMembers participate in weekly division-specific curriculum, technical workshops, speaker events, mentorship opportunities, and hands-on projects designed to develop both professional and leadership skills.\n\nCMC currently offers programming in Investment Banking \u0026 Private Equity, Equity Research, Sales \u0026 Trading, and Private Wealth Management. The organization also offers the Accelerator Program, an intensive technical and recruiting preparation program designed to help freshmen build foundational finance and recruiting skills.\n\nCMC recruits during both the Fall and Spring semesters, with recruiting typically taking place within the first few weeks of each semester. Interested students can learn more and apply at https://cmciu.com.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133490","key":"cba","name":"Chinese Business Association","shortName":"CBA","summary":"Chinese Business Association is an organization that prepares you to become a future business leader.","description":"The Chinese Business Association (CBA) is an academic, professional, and social organization. We aim to build communication and cooperation among members by encouraging and developing networks with students, alumni, faculty, and industry elite and by promoting knowledge about Chinese business culture in the IU community. We prepare our members for success in the business world by exposing them to a wide spectrum of industries and by providing resources to help with their careers. We cater to Chinese students who wish to be a part of the American business world and reach out to all individuals from different majors and ethnicities.\n\nIf you want to join CBA as a General Member, please follow us on our WeChat account \"CBA 印大商学会\" and attend one of our events. If you don\u0027t have a WeChat account, you can also follow us Instagram and LinkedIn. You can also send out an email to one of our board members to reach out.","categories":["Academic and Professional","International and Multicultural","Social","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133683","key":"cldatiu","name":"Civic Leadership Development","shortName":"CLD","summary":"Civic Leadership Development\n\nCivic Leadership Development (CLD) provides a wide array of opportunities for students to gain leadership skills through hands-on volunteerism in the local community and direct contact with non-profit leaders.","description":"**IMPORTANT MEMBERSHIP INFORMATION** Contact us via email or on Instagram at \"cldiu\" to join our GroupMe and to get connected!\n\nCivic Leadership Development (CLD) provides a wide array of opportunities for Kelley students to gain leadership skills through hands-on volunteerism in the local community and direct contact with leaders in the non-profit sector. While you are encouraged to stay active and be involved, CLD allows you to contribute, even if you are able to commit only a few hours each semester. The breadth of available long-term and shorter-term opportunities provides flexibility to match with your personal goals and availability. Options to be involved include direct community service, fundraising, and leadership experience. In addition, you can participate in and attend informational meetings, lectures, and other educational events.\n\nJoin our GroupMe!: https://groupme.com/join_group/116794939/1333heLo","categories":["Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133326","key":"ceoatiu","name":"Collegiate Entrepreneurs\u0027 Organization at IU","shortName":"CEO at IU","summary":"CEO is the premier entrepreneurship organization for IU students. We help aspiring entrepreneurs achieve their goals by connecting them with local resources to further their ideas and providing the training needed to successfully launch a business.","description":"The Collegiate Entrepreneurs\u0027 Organization (CEO) is IU\u0027s largest entrepreneurship organization dedicated to empowering members with professional, valuable information in an innovative, intuitive way. We are a family of student entrepreneurs from all backgrounds and areas of study to learn and develop the skills necessary for entrepreneurship. Our organization helps students of all future aspirations cultivate their entrepreneurial mindset, supports the entrepreneurial efforts of its members, and promotes entrepreneurial spirit across campus. This student organization was founded in 2001 as the Young Entrepreneurs Association and became a chapter of CEO in 2013. CEO at IU works closely with student organizations across campus to extend entrepreneurship\u0027s campus-wide influence in many diverse areas. CEO meets regularly to allow young entrepreneurs opportunities to network with peers, mentors, and successful business leaders.\n\nCEO Details:\n\nTime: Mondays from 7-8 pm\n\nLocation: Von Lee Entrepreneurship Center (above Noodles \u0026 Co. on Kirkwood)\n\nInstagram: @ceo.iu (This is where you will get the most up-to-date information on CEO club meetings, announcements, events, and more!)\n\nOther resources: LinkTree, Linked In\n\nWhat kind of events do we have?\n- Entrepreneurial Speakers \u0026 Workshops\n- Pitch Competitions \u0026 Idea Competitions\n- Cross-campus Club collaborations\n- Entrepreneurial Skill Development\n\nCEO is open and welcoming to all IU students.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"387256","key":"clc","name":"Corporate Law Club","shortName":"CLC","summary":"In CLC, we host a variety of guest speakers, host case competitions, and offer insight into law school admissions. Through case studies, guest speakers, \u0026 a plethora of questions and collaborative talks, students can gain law/business knowledge.","description":"In the corporate law club, we aim to build on professional traits of students looking to learn more about law and its involvement with business.\n\nThrough a variety of activities such as guest speakers, networking events, resume building, and law school admissions cycles- students will gain insight knowledge into the world of law and its implications.\n\nCorporate law club is also aimed at creating a community for students in which they can be competitive with a team. We look to host a variety of competitions based on recent events, mergers and acquisitions, and fictitious cases we\r\n will prepare for students in order to truly prepare for law school or whatever course of business they’d like to pursue.\n\nIn joining the CLC, students will learn valuable skills in legal studies as well as gain connections and network with guests and peers. As a club focused on professional growth, we will also help students build adequate resumes and\r\n improve their profiles online as they progress as learners and people.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Advocacy and Political","Governance","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"424268","key":"cc","name":"Credit Club","shortName":"CC","summary":"Credit Club is a student-led organization that forms opportunities for students to learn about the field of credit. We are intermediaries between students and top-level professionals with speaker meetings, workshops, and case competitions.","description":"Credit Club is dedicated to introducing underclassmen to the foundational principles that shape the world of credit. By serving as a bridge between students, experienced upperclassmen, and industry professionals, we provide accessible, high-quality education that empowers members to build strong financial and analytical skills. Through upperclassmen-led lectures, hands-on guidance, and insights from professional speakers, we aim to cultivate a supportive learning environment where students can grow into confident, informed members of the credit community.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"404786","key":"crimsonbusinessjournal","name":"Crimson Business Journal","shortName":"CBJ","summary":"The Crimson Business Journal connects students with current business events, offering a platform to develop writing, analytical, and critical thinking skills.","description":"The Crimson Business Journal is an organization dedicated to bridging the gap between current events in the business world and the perspectives of college students. By providing a platform for students to showcase their analytical and writing skills, CBJ fosters a dynamic environment where writers can engage with contemporary issues, develop critical thinking abilities, and refine their communication talents. Through its semesterly newsletter, CBJ fosters thoughtful analysis and insightful commentary, providing writers with the opportunity to contribute to key discussions within the business community. We will have several different coverage groups for our motivated writers to become involved in, which include technology, real estate, healthcare, stock analysis, international business, mergers and acquisitions, and economic analysis.\n\nPlease Apply Here","categories":["Academic and Professional","Z - Works with Children","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"419720","key":"cigatiu","name":"Crimson Investment Group","shortName":"CIG","summary":"The Premier Student-Managed Investment Fund at Indiana University","description":"Founded in March 2025, Crimson Investment Group, an KSO, upholds a high standard of intellectual curiosity, collaboration, and continuous improvement. Our members receive a realistic investing experience backed by rigorous training and exposure to industry professionals. CIG sets its analysts up for success through its representation in and partnerships with major investment banks and asset managers. Please note our recruiting cycle starts at the beginning of each semester. Follow our instagram @cigatiu for updates!","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"228679","key":"dv","name":"Data Visualization at IU","shortName":"DV @ IU","summary":"The mission of Data Visualization at IU is to equip students with the technical and analytical skills needed to solve business problems through data and technology.","description":"Data Visualization at Indiana University provides organizations and students with high-quality, practical solutions through the power of data. We work with members to develop hands-on skills in data manipulation and visualization, equipping them to tackle real-world business challenges.\n\nData Visualization connects the untapped potential of Kelley students with the growing demand for data-driven decision-making. Importantly, the process is mutually beneficial. Students gain experience with platforms like Tableau, Power BI, and Salesforce, develop leadership and professional skills through workshops, alumni meetings, resume reviews, and corporate interactions, and have the opportunity to make a measurable impact. Organizations benefit from innovative, data-backed solutions that help them make informed decisions and achieve their goals.\n\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/dvatiu/\n\nFall 2026 Application: https://forms.gle/1E2M84q6kRpQ8wLh9","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Technology, Data, + Analytics","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"406646","key":"collegiate-deca-at-indiana-university-bloomington","name":"DECA at Indiana University Bloomington","shortName":"DECA at Indiana University Bloomington","summary":"A student organization focused on professional development through workshops, competitions, and leadership activities. Helping members gain experience and prepare for collegiate DECA events in fields like marketing, finance, hospitality, and management.","description":"Collegiate DECA at Indiana University Bloomington is a student organization dedicated to promoting professional development and preparing students for their future careers. Through workshops, competitions, and networking opportunities, members build skills in marketing, finance, hospitality, and management. Our organization provides a platform for students to compete in Collegiate DECA events, connect with industry professionals, and engage in leadership activities, all while gaining real-world experience to excel in business and beyond.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Z - Works with Children","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133590","key":"dsp","name":"Delta Sigma Pi","shortName":"DSP","summary":"Delta Sigma Pi is a professional fraternity comprised of business-focused students growing together through professional events, community service opportunities, strong networks, and a diverse brotherhood full of friendship and lifelong bonds.","description":"Delta Sigma Pi is a professional fraternity organized to foster the study of business in universities; to encourage scholarship, social activity and the association of students for their mutual advancement by research and practice; to promote a closer affiliation between the commerical world and students of commerce, and to futher a higher standard of commercial ethics and culture and the civic and commercial welfare of the community.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","Service and Philanthropy","Z - New Member Training","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133349","key":"emergingleadersinstitute","name":"Emerging Leaders Institute","shortName":"ELI","summary":"Leading with purpose, growing with passion.","description":"The Emerging Leaders Institute strives to empower students by fostering an environment that emphasizes leadership development and professional growth. Through a combination of workshops, seminars, leadership training, corporate partnerships, and community engagement, we aim to equip members with the skills and experiences necessary to become impactful and innovative leaders in their future careers.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"331499","key":"epsilonnutau","name":"Epsilon Nu Tau","shortName":"ENT","summary":"Epsilon Nu Tau is a professional fraternity which inspires the growth of entrepreneurial minds and professional development, while providing a tight-knit community for its brothers.","description":"Epsilon Nu Tau is the fastest growing business fraternity on campus. We pride ourselves in our four pillars of brotherhood, ethics, accountability, and innovation.\n\nThrough our focus on entrepreneurship, ENT brothers have exciting corporate visits, a KPMG corporate sponsorship, and events such as a Shark Tank pitch competition and a business launch project. You can find our brothers around campus playing intramural sports and chatting at the SPEA library. ENT serves a greater purpose than just a professional network-we are truly a family, supporting and motivating our brothers in all their endeavors.\n\nIt is our goal to ensure our members receive the proper mentorship and experience to achieve their professional goals. Our network mixed with our brotherhood contributes to a collaborative environment that provides our actives with the resources and opportunities necessary to succeed.\n\nEpsilon Nu Tau is an application-based organization and any requests to join through BeInvolved will be denied. Check out our website for more recruitment information! entbloom.com/recruitment","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"341232","key":"financialinvestmentreview","name":"Financial Investment Review","shortName":"FIR","summary":"The Financial Investment Review (FIR) is an undergraduate student organization at Indiana University. Our goal is to prepare our students for careers in the financial services industry and to help our members learn about key concepts and skills.","description":"","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133574","key":"fsc","name":"Financial Services Club","shortName":"FSC","summary":"The Financial Services Club is the official undergraduate organization at Kelley for students interested in careers within the financial services industry.","description":"The Financial Services Club (FSC) is the official undergraduate organization at Kelley for students considering careers in:\n- Investment Banking \n- Sales \u0026 Trading \n- Private Wealth Management \n- Equity Research \n- Capital Markets \n- Corporate Banking \n\nLed by workshop members, faculty workshop\r\n directors, and industry professionals, the club provides an overview of the financial services industry and practical experiences intended to prepare students for workshop applications.\n\nNo need to apply for membership, join the FSC Canvas page: https://iu.instructure.com/enroll/936GAM","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"330002","key":"fintechiu","name":"FinTech at Indiana University","shortName":"FT@IU","summary":"Fintech at Indiana University seeks to connect finance/business students with computer science students to create a powerful array of skills that are both practical, translatable, and powerful when entering the workforce.","description":"Stay Connected:\n\nhttps://groupme.com/join_group/96345040/FTlx9aAB\n\nMission statement:\nFinTech @ IU is a student organization whose core belief is that business and computer science is one of the most powerful combinations of study. We blend the skills of our members to create more well-rounded individuals. \n\nDescription:\nFinTech at Indiana University aims to create a community that will be involved in an interactive learning approach about concepts, terms, and companies in the FinTech sector through weekly or bi-weekly discussion sessions, guest speaker sessions, monthly or bi-monthly research papers, collaborative events with clubs within and outside of Indiana University, and a uniquely formatted case competition.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"334663","key":"firstgenerationinvestors","name":"First Generation Investors","shortName":"FGI","summary":"First Generation Investors (FGI) is a non-profit 501(c)3 organization where college students tutor high school students in underserved communities the power of investing and brings classroom lessons to life by providing students real money to invest.","description":"First Generation Investors (FGI) is a non-profit 501(c)3 organization where college students tutor high school students in underserved communities the power of investing and brings classroom lessons to life by providing students real money to invest.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Service and Philanthropy","Z - Works with Children","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"292074","key":"fblaatiu","name":"Future Business Leaders of America at Indiana University Bloomington","shortName":"FBLA at IU Bloomington","summary":"Future Business Leaders of America (FBLA) is a national student organization that prepares members for careers in business through leadership development, career exploration, academic competitions, and networking opportunities.","description":"Future Business Leaders of America (FBLA) at Indiana University Bloomington is a collegiate chapter of the nation’s premier student business organization. FBLA’s mission is to prepare students for careers in business through academic competitions,\r\n leadership development, networking opportunities, and professional growth experiences. Members participate in state and national conferences, case competitions, and skill-based events across all areas of business, from finance and marketing to technology and\r\n management.\n\nOur chapter at IU Bloomington will carry forward these opportunities while establishing a\r\nspecial focus on entrepreneurship. In partnership with IU Innovates and other campus resources, we will host workshops, speaker sessions, and discussions that explore the realities of building and scaling a business. Students will gain hands-on\r\n insights into startup development, decision-making, and leadership that extend beyond entrepreneurship into all business fields. Whether preparing to launch a venture or pursuing a career in a traditional industry, members will develop adaptable skills and\r\n a strong professional network to support their future success.\n\nJoin our Free Slack Community!: \r\nSlack\n\nSubscribe to our newsletter to stay up-to-date!\n\nFBLA at IU-Bloomington Substack","categories":["Academic and Professional","Service and Philanthropy","Z - Travel - International","Z - Works with Children","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"346140","key":"fph","name":"Future Professionals in Healthcare","shortName":"FPH","summary":"Future Professionals in Healthcare provides students with the opportunity to learn and network with those experienced in the healthcare administration, medical management, and business sectors of the life science industries.","description":"Future Professionals in Healthcare (FPH) is an interdisciplinary student organization based in the Kelley School of Business and the O’Neill School of Public and Environmental Affairs. Our mission is to develop the next generation of healthcare leaders who will drive innovation and reform across the healthcare system.\n\nThrough three core tracks - Healthcare Management and Policy, Healthcare Finance and Systems, and Healthcare Innovation, Entrepreneurship, and Technology - we offer hands-on projects, speaker events, workshops, and professional development opportunities that prepare students to lead at the intersection of business, policy, and medicine.\n\nWe believe that true impact happens through collaboration across disciplines, and our vision is to create a community of students empowered to tackle healthcare’s most pressing challenges with bold, system-level solutions.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"375644","key":"llmsinbusiness","name":"Generative AI and LLMs in Business","shortName":null,"summary":"Democratizing AI literacy across Indiana University | Learn more at https://genaiiu.com/","description":"Welcome / About the Club\n\nClub Overview\nGen. AI Club is a student-led learning organization at Indiana University dedicated to advancing AI education across disciplines. Our community provides structured opportunities for members from all academic backgrounds to explore, build, and apply AI ethically, accessibly, and impactfully.\n\nMembers will:\n- \r\nParticipate in projects and hands-on AI applications\n- \r\nLearn AI theory, tools, and ethical frameworks\n- \r\nNetwork with peers, faculty, alumni, and industry professionals\n- \r\nEngage in workshops, guest speakers, and semester-long initiatives\n\nHow to Join\n\nStudents interested in joining the Generative AI and LLMs for Business Club must complete a written application and submit a current resume during the designated recruitment period. Students can find the link to the application on our website, social media, QR codes on posters, and at our callout meeting at the beginning of each semester. Applications are reviewed by the organization’s leadership team, and selected applicants may be invited to participate in an interview process. Interviews are conducted to evaluate applicants’ interest in the club, commitment to participation, and alignment with the organization’s mission and values. Admission decisions are made following the completion of the interview process. Students accepted into the organization must then complete registration through the Indiana University student organization platform to be recognized as official members. \n\nMission \u0026 Vision\n\nMission\nGen. AI Club develops interdisciplinary student leaders capable of understanding, building, and evaluating AI systems critically. Members gain technical fluency in AI frameworks, computational tools, and system design while emphasizing ethical reasoning, governance awareness, and human-centered decision-making.\n\nVision\nBy 2027, Gen. AI Club aims to be a leading campus community for AI education, providing members with the skills and ethical framework to influence AI use across industries, policy, and research.\n\nCore Principles / Pillars\n- \r\nFoster Inquiry: Define impactful AI problems\n- \r\nEnable Knowledge: Build technical and ethical skills\n- \r\nDrive Collaboration: Implement AI solutions in teams\n- \r\nEnsure Ethics: Evaluate societal and human impact\n- \r\nAmplify Learning: Share insights and mentor members\n\nSocial Media \u0026 Staying Connected\n- Website: genaiiu.com\n- \r\nInstagram: @genaiiu\n- \r\nLinkedIn: @Gen AI Club at IU \n- \r\nEmail: admin@genaiiu.com","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133526","key":"gbbatiu","name":"Global Business Brigades at Indiana University","shortName":"GBB at IU","summary":"Global Business Brigades at Indiana University","description":"Global Business Brigades at Indiana University strives to create a level of sustainability in developing economies across the world. They do this by consulting microenterprises on week-long trips to rural areas of countries outside the United States, including Honduras, Panama, Nicaragua, Ghana, Greece, Belize, etc. Students are able to learn about diverse cultures while teaching community members basic knowledge of business concepts learned here at Indiana University.","categories":["Academic and Professional","International and Multicultural","Service and Philanthropy","Z - Travel - International","IU Kelley School of Business","Alternative Break Experiences","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"378921","key":"hispanicfinanceassociation","name":"Hispanic Finance Association","shortName":"HFA","summary":"The Hispanic Finance Association (HFA) a student-run organization focused on helping undergrads land competitive jobs. HFA hopes to increase hispanic representation and inspire character in the next generation of leaders.","description":"The Hispanic Finance Association (HFA) is a dynamic and influential organization dedicated to advancing the representation and success of Hispanic individuals within the finance industry. Founded on the principles of diversity, inclusion, and professional development, HFA empowers Hispanic professionals and students to thrive in the world of finance while fostering a supportive community that celebrates Hispanic heritage.\n\nKey Initiatives and Objectives:\n- \r\nNetworking and Community Building: HFA brings together Hispanic finance professionals, students, and industry leaders through networking events, conferences, and online platforms. We facilitate connections that inspire collaboration and career growth.\n- \r\nProfessional Development: We offer a range of resources, including workshops, seminars, and mentorship programs, to enhance the skills and knowledge of our members. HFA is committed to nurturing talent and fostering career advancement. We also partner with firms in the financial services industry such as Warburg Pincus, Bank of America, Insight Partners and more!\n- Scholarships and Education: Through scholarships, educational programs, and case competitions with monetary prizes HFA supports Hispanic students pursuing careers in finance. These programs help compliment classroom knowledge to prepare for interviews and internships.\n\nGroupMe: https://groupme.com/join_group/101236108/V6DQJ91L","categories":["Academic and Professional","International and Multicultural","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"333884","key":"hcn","name":"Hoosier Consulting Network","shortName":"HCN","summary":"Hoosier Consulting Network is a Kelley SGSO and consulting organization dedicated to advancing collaboration between ambitious Indiana University students and small businesses, startups, government entities, and nonprofits in the local Indiana community.","description":"Hoosier Consulting Network is a Kelley SGSO and consulting organization dedicated to advancing collaboration between ambitious Indiana University students and small businesses, startups, government entities, and nonprofits in the local Indiana community. Our goal is to provide robust, and timely solutions for our clients while simultaneously helping our consultants develop strong cross-functional teamwork skills.\n\nHCN connects students with real clients and challenging cases. Our contract-based consulting projects will be assigned to a team based on its aptitude, experience, availability, and interest. Project duration is flexible and you will be exposed to working on a variety of cross-functional projects. Every team will be led by the Project Team Leader who will ensure the smooth operation of the teams, and ultimately client satisfaction.\n\nWe are looking for passionate problem-solvers who possess a dynamic skill set and can collaborate with their diverse team members to deliver quality outcomes that meet the high standards of our clients. This is an incredible opportunity to gain exposure to consulting in the real world while contributing to the under-serviced part of our local community.\n\nOur application opens on our Instagram at the start of every semester. \n\nHCN Linktree: https://linktr.ee/hoosierconsultingnetwork","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"387570","key":"isbaatiu","name":"Indian Student Business Association","shortName":"ISBA ","summary":"ISBA\u0027s vision is to cultivate a lasting ecosystem at Indiana University that connects students, alumni, and professionals, empowering all undergraduate students to shape their professional growth through mentorship, collaboration, and unique experiences.","description":"The Indian Student Business Association exists to empower undergraduate students of Indian heritage, culture, and identity at Indiana University, regardless of major, to explore business through professional development,\r\n mentorship, and hands-on opportunities. ISBA creates a community where students are kept at the forefront of all initiatives and are encouraged to grow through collaboration, diverse perspectives, and real-world experiences.","categories":["Academic and Professional","International and Multicultural","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133232","key":"ibaatiu","name":"International Business Association","shortName":"IBA at IU","summary":"The International Business Association is an organization focused on complementing the International Business major, for students interested in international business issues and career opportunities around the world.","description":"The International Business Association at Indiana University is an organization dedicated to exposing students to the business world beyond the US borders. \n\nWork with students from around the globe and join a growing club devoted to building students\u0027 international profiles. With events like workshops on landing international internships, meetings with professionals from around the world, and cultural events, you can become the well-rounded professional multinational corporations seek to recruit. \n\nPlease join the GroupMe https://groupme.com/join_group/89717930/NAha1XIb for regular updates and details of upcoming events (open to everyone)!","categories":["Academic and Professional","International and Multicultural","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","IU Maurer School of Law","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"425182","key":"internationalfinanceandbankingclub","name":"International Finance \u0026 Banking Club","shortName":null,"summary":"The International Finance and Banking Club educates students on investment banking and finance careers with a global focus, exploring international markets and career paths through workshops, speakers, and skill-based programs.","description":"The purpose of the International Finance and Banking Club is to educate students about investment banking and finance careers with a strong emphasis on international financial markets. The organization provides insight into\r\n how investment banking operates across major global financial centers, highlighting differences in market structures, recruiting processes, professional expectations, and career paths. Through workshops, speaker events, and skill-based programming, the club\r\n equips members with the technical knowledge and global perspective needed to pursue finance opportunities across international markets.","categories":["Academic and Professional","International and Multicultural","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"386424","key":"ipo_investing_at_iu","name":"IPO Investing at IU","shortName":null,"summary":"IPO Investing at IU is an organization that holds discussions about companies that recently went public and private companies planning to go public. At each meeting, members discuss a different company and decide if it would be a good investment.","description":"IPO Investing at IU is an organization that holds discussions about companies that recently went public and private companies planning to go public. At each meeting, a different group of members gives a brief presentation about a company of their choice. After that, members discuss the company\u0027s finances, corporate strategy, room for growth, etc. and end the meeting by voting on whether or not the company would be a good investment. IPO Investing at IU gives club members the chance to learn more about investing and corporate strategy, in addition to providing leadership and professional development opportunities.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133649","key":"kep","name":"Kappa Eta Phi Professional Fraternity","shortName":"KEP","summary":"Kappa Eta Phi is a Professional Fraternity established to promote the importance of professional academic study in the university, expand members\u0027 professional networking experience, and maintain lasting friendships amongst brothers and sisters.","description":"Kappa Eta Phi is dedicated to fostering professional, academic, and social excellence within the University community. Through enriching networking opportunities and the cultivation of enduring bonds among members, both professionally and socially, Kappa Eta Phi elevates the collegiate experience. Additionally, KEP is committed to advancing cultural and ethical standards within the university environment, ensuring our members are prepared to make meaningful contributions to society.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"388585","key":"kappaomegaalpha","name":"Kappa Omega Alpha","shortName":"KOA","summary":"The goal of KOA is bring together students interested in business, law, and public policy to build a community that offers professional, social, and service opportunities with the goal of developing members into professionals and leaders","description":"Kappa Omega Alpha Co-ed Fraternity is dedicated to supporting undergraduates interested in business, law, and public policy. Through networking, workshops, and community service, we foster academic and professional growth while promoting fraternal bonds and upholding our core values. Our commitment to inclusivity and excellence shapes a vibrant community of leaders dedicated to making a positive impact.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"407323","key":"kappathetapi","name":"Kappa Theta Pi","shortName":"KTP","summary":"Kappa Theta Pi is a professional technology fraternity that fosters a community of driven students through networking, mentorship, social events and skill-building. It prepares members for success in the tech industry while building lifelong connections.","description":"Kappa Theta Pi is a professional technology fraternity that connects ambitious students with a shared passion for technology and innovation. The fraternity fosters a dynamic community where members have access to networking opportunities, workshops, and\r\n career resources. From engaging with industry professionals through events to attending skill-building workshops, KTP provides the tools needed to excel both academically and professionally.\n\nBeyond career development, KTP encourages members to grow through competitive technical events like hackathons, coding challenges, and team projects. These events help members improve their technical skills while promoting collaboration within the fraternity.\r\n KTP also offers a fun and supportive environment with social events and team-building activities, ensuring members have a well-rounded experience and build lasting friendships and professional connections.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","Z - New Member Training","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133407","key":"ksg","name":"Kelley Student Government","shortName":"KSG","summary":"Kelley Student Government (KSG) is a voice for Kelley students, a body to run initiatives and enhance experiences, and the bridge between administration and the Kelley student organizations.","description":"Serving as the link between Kelley students, faculty, and administration, our purpose is to enhance the student experience at Kelley, foster an inclusive and innovative environment, and influence positive change. In order to represent the Kelley School\u0027s diverse student body, voting members include both general delegates and organization representatives. KSG is comprised of the following committees:\n- Academic Experience\n- Alumni Engagement\n- DEIJB\n- Ethics \u0026 Social Responsibility\n- Funding\n- Health \u0026 Wellbeing\n- Internal Development\n- Marketing\n- Professional Development\n- Student Life\n- Undergraduate Research","categories":["Academic and Professional","Advocacy and Political","Governance","IU Kelley School of Business","University Student Organization (USO)","BL-USO"]},{"id":"133338","key":"kfs","name":"Korean Finance Seminar","shortName":"KFS","summary":"Corporate Finance, Case Analysis, Investment Banking, Commercial Banking, Financial Services, Consulting","description":"Korean Finance Seminar helps high-potential undergraduates at Indiana University Bloomington establish placement as entry-level analysts with respectable firms in the financial services industry. Korea Finance Seminar is a mini-workshop experience and is an intensive ten-week seminar where students learn about various financial topics and discuss current events. Korean Finance Seminar participants learn to \"play the game\" by demonstrating how financial intermediary firms apply the theory these students learn in their core courses.\n\nLink: http://iukfs.weebly.com/","categories":["Academic and Professional","International and Multicultural","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"370102","key":"limitlessclubatiu","name":"Limitless Club at IU","shortName":"Limitless","summary":"Limitless Club fosters an entrepreneurial mindset by providing ambitious people with the platform, resources, and network to turn their inspiring pursuits into tangible reality.","description":"A group of like-minded, highly-motivated, and goal oriented entrepreneurs, artists, and creators who aim to live life on their own terms. The club will feature different events, guest speakers, and challenges designed to empower members to develop an entrepreneurial mindset and accomplish personal and professional goals no matter what they are. Members will learn skills such as critical thinking, entrepreneurship, collaboration, problem solving, habit building, financial literacy and so much more.  Come join a group of students working together to accomplish their goals while laying the foundation for a successful career and life. Club meetings are twice a month with some spontaneous events and challenges throughout the semester. Time commitment is between 4-8 hours per month.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"367554","key":"maa","name":"M\u0026A Advisors at IU","shortName":null,"summary":"M\u0026A Advisors at Indiana provides students with exposure to the various advisory roles in the mergers and acquisitions process.","description":"M\u0026A Advisors at Indiana provides students with exposure to the various advisory roles in the mergers and acquisitions process (Investment Banking, Consulting, etc). Our two verticals, Finance and Strategy, encompass every facet of M\u0026A. In joining this organization, students will undergo intensive hands-on lectures which equip them with the technical skillset of an analyst in that field. \n\nPlease visit our Instagram account at https://www.instagram.com/maadvisorsiu for all recruiting information.\n\nOur Spring 2026 Application is now CLOSED as of Sunday, 1/25/26 at 11:59PM. Our Fall 2026 Applications will open in August.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133487","key":"mubetalambda","name":"Mu Beta Lambda Business Fraternity, Inc.","shortName":"Mu Beta Lambda","summary":"Mu Beta Lambda is a revolutionary organization of educated minorities that empower one another. As young professionals, we utilize our network to create opportunities for the advancement of our members as well as our community.","description":"Mu Beta Lambda, the nation\u0027s first minority business fraternity, is a business fraternity founded on February 17, 2012 on the campus of Indiana University. The charter members wanted to bring diverse students passionate about business and improving professional\r\n skills into a community that could strengthen one another through college and beyond. With our pillars of kinship, diversity and culture, professionalism, scholarship, and community, we have been able to see our members gain internships, leadership positions,\r\n and full-time job offers before graduation. We are open to all majors with an emphasis on business. Each year, we are growing and improving to become the business leaders of tomorrow. Our latest endeavor is incorporating sustainability into our organization\r\n and members.","categories":["Academic and Professional","International and Multicultural","Service and Philanthropy","Z - New Member Training","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133614","key":"netimpact","name":"Net Impact: Sustainable Business Club","shortName":"Net Impact","summary":"Connecting students with hands-on consulting projects, sustainability initiatives, and professional development to drive meaningful impact.","description":"Net Impact at Indiana University is a professional organization dedicated to developing future leaders in sustainability and social impact. Through impact consulting, corporate partnerships, professional development, and community engagement, we equip students to solve real-world business challenges that create lasting environmental, social, and economic value.\n\nMembers gain hands-on experience through sustainability consulting projects, networking events, career workshops, social events, sustainable education events, and volunteer initiatives while building the analytical, leadership, and problem-solving skills needed to create meaningful impact across industries.\n\nWe meet Mondays from 7:00–8:00 PM in Hodge Hall and host additional networking, volunteer, and social events throughout the semester. Follow @netimpact_iu on Instagram or join our GroupMe to stay connected. Also Join our newsletter to learn what we\u0027re doing every week!","categories":["Academic and Professional","Environmental and Sustainability","Service and Philanthropy","Z - Travel","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"420838","key":"nextstepnetworking","name":"Next Step Networking","shortName":"NSN","summary":"Our vision for Next Step Networking is to foster a community of people who want to get outside of their comfort zone. We are creating NSN to improve our interpersonal, communicating, presenting, interview, and conversational skills.","description":"Our vision for Next Step Networking is to foster a community of people who want to get outside of their comfort zone. We are creating an NSN to improve our interpersonal, communication, presentation, interview, and conversational skills. A meeting at NSN might entail a focused conversation, where we create stimulating topics intended to encourage members to have deep and thoughtful discussions about their career goals, fears, dreams, and more. Outside of these focused conversations, we will do presentations too about various schools of thought, goals, and similar topics. Sometimes members will be able to prepare for the topic before the day, other times they will have to be spontaneous . Whether we\u0027re doing spontaneous TedTalks or discussion this combination of several forms/types of communication skills will elevate members so they are ready to break their mental barriers and get rid of any social fears. By doing these together, we will become a collection of professional and confident college students ready for the workplace.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133512","key":"pct","name":"Phi Chi Theta Professional Fraternity","shortName":"PCT","summary":"Phi Chi Theta is a co-educational professional fraternity dedicated to fostering personal and professional growth of our brotherhood through leadership, diversity, and philanthropy.","description":"Since being founded in 2009, the Zeta Eta chapter has continued to grow and develop, while staying true to our five core values of Professionalism, Leadership, Philanthropy, Diversity, and Brotherhood. \n\nThe Zeta Eta chapter places a strong foundation on leadership in each of its brothers; our members are not only dedicated to their brothers in Phi Chi Theta, but also to developing as leaders by holding positions in the fraternity. Internally, 40% of our members hold leadership positions in Phi Chi Theta. Not only has our brothers continued to make great leadership strides within the fraternity, but have also shown impressive reaches in academic elements. We are proud to have our brothers excel inside the classroom and in our fraternity. Our members accomplishments include Founder’s Scholars, Kelley Honors students, various case competition finalists, and many others. We believe that this strong push for leadership in all aspects of our college career allows every brother to develop the strategic skills necessary to excel in the future. Placement includes Deloitte, EY, PWC, Citi, United Airlines, Jefferies, FTI, Accenture, etc. \n\nWe aim to give back to our supporting community by organizing and participating in philanthropic events every year. We have established, and continued to foster, a relationship with Big Brothers Big Sisters in Bloomington and organize events in the Fall and Spring for them each year. Over this past academic year, with our base of 93 active members we had over a consistent 85% participation on all community service events at organizations in the surrounding area of Bloomington, such as Community Kitchen, Wheeler Mission Ministries, SCAAP. In addition, our member base found new ways to stay involved even with the pandemic through digital means, such as writing letters to people in nursing homes and St. Jude and working with Hope for Justice. By fostering these ongoing philanthropic relationships, our brothers continue to develop individually while helping to serve our local communities.\n\nWe look forward to continuous growth, innovation, and dedication internally, as well as in all of our professional pursuits. We are enthusiastic about continuing to adapt our professional skills and knowledge to the ever-changing standards, and we strive to continue to produce the most professional, achieving individuals to emerge into the professional workplace.\n\nPlease check out our website and Instagram for rush information!","categories":["Academic and Professional","Service and Philanthropy","Z - New Member Training","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133563","key":"pgn","name":"Phi Gamma Nu","shortName":"PGN","summary":"Phi Gamma Nu is a premiere nationally recognized business fraternity where we promote ownership and innovation as the avenue for leadership development.","description":"Established in 2014, Phi Gamma Nu – Delta Psi is a premiere business fraternity at Indiana University. As a Chapter of a national organization founded on the pillars of Professionalism, Philanthropy, and Community; we are committed to fostering a diverse\r\n network of innovative members. Fueled by the passions of our individual members and united by a shared business mindset, we are shaping the industry leaders of tomorrow.\n\nOur recruitment takes places at the beginning of the fall and spring semester every year. The best place to find information on recruitment and what we are up to will always be our Instagram: @pgniub or our website:\n\niupgn.com. We look forward to meeting you!","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"168041","key":"pse","name":"Pi Sigma Epsilon","shortName":"PSE","summary":"PSE is a National Business Fraternity that is open to all IU students regardless of major. We are looking for students who want to make their mark on this university and leave with the skills to succeed in business.","description":"Pi Sigma Epsilon at Indiana University is a prestigious co-ed business fraternity dedicated to the comprehensive growth of its members. With a primary focus on both professional and social development, PSE offers a wide range of leadership roles where students can take charge of their growth and contribute to the fraternity’s development. Through a variety of activities, including professional development workshops, networking events with corporate sponsors, and community service initiatives, members are equipped with the skills and experiences necessary for success in their future careers. PSE cultivates its familial and close-knit community through a multitude of social events, including formals, an annual chapter-wide trip, alumni dinners, and more. Through this organization, members are exposed to a one-of-a-kind brotherhood built on support to foster lifelong friendships and guidance to achieve their professional goals.\n\nIf you\u0027d like to learn more about our recruitment process, please check out or social media\u0027s or reach out directly to JJ Viswanathan (jviswana@iu.edu).","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133240","key":"portfoliomanagementclub","name":"Portfolio Management Club","shortName":"PMC","summary":"Portfolio Management Club (PMC) is Indiana University\u0027s largest discussion-based finance organization.","description":"Portfolio Management Club (PMC) is Indiana University\u0027s largest discussion-based finance organization. Members meet weekly to discuss the financial markets from a variety of perspectives applicable to careers in investing and advisory. The Portfolio Management Club prides itself on developing member skill sets rooted in developing and defending an opinion, an often-understated attribute amongst undergraduate finance students. Club alumni have gone on to pursue roles at leading investment banks, hedge funds, and private equity firms.\n\nPortfolio Management Club welcomes new members every semester, though application cycles are highly competitive. The Spring 2026 application cycle has ended and will reopen in the fall.\n\n*Use your IU email to access the application*\n\nOur callout meeting will be hosted closer to the next application cycle.\n\nPlease see our official website, kelleypmc.org, for more information.\n\nNOTE: Clicking join on BeInvolved will not result in admittance to Portfolio Management Club.\n\nIf you have any questions, you can email the leadership team here.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"387106","key":"qfsiu","name":"Quantitative Finance Society","shortName":"QFS @IU","summary":"The Quantitative Finance Society at Indiana University is a dynamic and forward-thinking student organization dedicated to enhancing the knowledge and skills of its members in the fields of economics, finance, statistics, mathematics, and coding.","description":"Fall 2026 Application Now Open\n\nThe Quantitative Finance Society at Indiana University is a dynamic and forward-thinking student organization dedicated to enhancing the knowledge and skills of its members in the fields of economics, finance, statistics, mathematics, and coding. With a strong commitment to academic and professional development, the society serves as a hub for students aspiring to excel in quantitative finance.\n\nOne of the primary objectives of the Quantitative Finance Society is to provide its members with a comprehensive understanding of the interdisciplinary aspects of quantitative finance. Through workshops, seminars, and collaborative learning initiatives, the society fosters an environment where students can deepen their expertise in quantitative methodologies and gain valuable insights into the intricacies of financial markets.\n\nA key focus of the society is to empower its members for success in both graduate school admissions and the workforce. By offering resources such as exam preparation materials, networking opportunities, and mentorship programs, the Quantitative Finance Society equips its members with the tools and support needed to pursue advanced studies or enter the professional arena with confidence.\n\nTo further enrich the learning experience, the society organizes monthly events featuring distinguished speakers from both industry and academia. These speakers share their expertise, experiences, and insights, providing members with a unique opportunity to connect with professionals and scholars in the field. The diverse range of topics covered in these sessions ensures that members gain a holistic understanding of the quantitative finance landscape.\n\nA standout initiative of the Quantitative Finance Society is the establishment of the quantitative fund. This ambitious project reflects the society\u0027s commitment to applying theoretical knowledge to real-world scenarios. Members are actively involved in developing and implementing trading strategies, utilizing the skills they have acquired through their academic pursuits. The quantitative fund not only serves as a practical application of the club\u0027s educational objectives but also opens up avenues for members to gain hands-on experience in managing financial portfolios.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133383","key":"reclubiu","name":"Real Estate Club at Indiana University","shortName":"RE Club at IU","summary":"The mission of our club is to provide members networking opportunities for internships and full-time employment, offer educational forums to familiarize members with various topics in commercial real estate. Fill out the application here: reclubatiu.com","description":"*To become a member please fill out the application on our website. \n\nThe Real Estate Club is an organization that was founded in 1990 to fulfill the needs of students wanting to learn more about the real estate industry. The club is affiliated with the IU Center for Real Estate Studies and Kelley School of Business on the Bloomington campus.\n\nThe mission of our club is to provide members networking opportunities for internships and full-time employment, offer educational forums to familiarize our members with career paths in real estate, encourage job shadowing events, promote mentorships, and establish relationships among members and sponsors. No prior knowledge or experience in real estate is needed in order to join the club. \n\nFor the 2021-2022 school year, The Real Estate Club at Indiana University was proud to be named Kelley Student Organization of the Year by Kelley Student Government out of 70+ Organizations!\n\nAny questions or concerns? Email the club at iureclub@gmail.com","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"378374","key":"rem-on-campus","name":"Rem on Campus","shortName":"Rem","summary":"The purpose of Rem on Campus is to create an engaging curriculum shaping students and young problem-solvers into the next generation of impact-driven innovators. Rem on Campus is a social impact initiative with pro-bono consulting engagement","description":"The purpose of Rem on Campus is to create an immersive curriculum shaping students and young problem-solvers into the next generation of impact-driven innovators. Rem on Campus is a way for students to develop new personal and professional relationships, engage in unique hands-on learning experiences, but most of all positively impact their community.  \n\nThis is achieved by having members engage directly with local businesses and nonprofits in the local community. Community engagements are normally six to eight week sprints where students identify opportunities for growth within a business or nonprofit and work together on teams to provide solutions. These services fall under pro-bono community consulting engagements. Students receive training and guidance from Rem and Company. Community engagements can also present themselves in the form of performing research, interviewing small businesses, writing articles, advocating for small businesses, etc.","categories":["Advocacy and Political","Arts and Entertainment","Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"342964","key":"rxdi","name":"Restructuring and Distressed Investing at IU","shortName":"RxDI","summary":"Restructuring and Distressed Investing (RxDI) is dedicated to providing education and preparation for the fields of distressed investing, advisory restructuring, and bankruptcy law.","description":"The Restructuring \u0026 Distressed Investing Club (RxDI) at Indiana University provides students with fundamental education and preparation for the fields of distressed investing, advisory restructuring, and bankruptcy law through our curriculum, mentorship, case competitions, and our student-led newsletter: The Cramdown.\n\nOur goal is to provide opportunities for members to grow, develop, and evolve into strong business leaders. We look to equip our members with the skills and opportunities needed to thrive in the industry, no matter their background or prior experience level.\n\nFor more information, join our GroupMe: HERE or see our website HERE\n\nAlso, follow this LINK to our application","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"409482","key":"rhoepsiloniota","name":"Rho Epsilon Iota - Upsilon Chapter","shortName":"REI","summary":"Rho Epsilon Iota fosters a collaborative brotherhood and unites students passionate about real estate. Through networking, mentorship, and workshops, we empower members with lasting connections and industry knowledge to excel in their careers.","description":"Rho Epsilon Iota is the nation’s first premier real estate fraternity, dedicated to fostering the next generation of real estate professionals by creating an inclusive environment for learning, growth, and professional development.\n\n2026-2027 Co-Presidents:\n\nBraden Yost — Senior Director of Commercial Real Estate\n\nJJ Baxter — Senior Director of Residential Real Estate\n\nOur Mission:\n- National Expansion: Become the future of professional real estate fraternities, nationally.\n- Inclusive Environment: Create a space for real estate minds to flourish regardless of prior experience.\n- Professional Advancement: Promote the professional advancement of all aspiring real estate professionals through commercial, residential, industrial, land, and special-use programs.\n- High Standards: Uphold the highest standards of honesty, equality, representation, knowledge, and professionalism on college campuses and within the community.\n\nCore Values:\n- Excellence: We strive for the highest standards in everything we do, both professionally and personally.\n- Brotherhood: We foster lasting bonds built on mutual respect, support, and shared commitment to success.\n- Growth: We believe in continuous learning, personal development, and pushing boundaries.\n- Service: We give back to our communities and invest in the next generation through the REI Impact Fund.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","University Student Organization (USO)","BL-USO"]},{"id":"142785","key":"salesclubksb","name":"Sales Club at Kelley","shortName":"Sales Club","summary":"Sales Club","description":"Have questions?  Contact us at saleclub@iu.edu.\n\n-\n\nReady to join Sales Club? \n\n1. Click \"JOIN\" Sales Club\n\nOnce completed, you\u0027ll be added to the Sales Club Canvas page which officially grants you membership!\n\n-\n\nThe Kelley Sales Club provides students with a comprehensive immersion in sales-focused activities. Open to freshmen through seniors from all majors, both within and outside the Kelley School of Business, members develop crucial skills for future sales leadership roles while gaining valuable experience to thrive in various career paths.\n\n-\n\nUnder the guidance of faculty advisor Dennis Spahr, the Sales Club is led by a student executive board that directs its initiatives. The club facilitates connections between students and corporate sales professionals, offering insights into real-world opportunities and challenges through sales competitions, round-table discussions, and networking events.\n\n-\n\nSee what we\u0027ve been up to:\n\nSales Club Instagram\n\nSales Club LinkedIn","categories":["IU Kelley School of Business","University Student Organization (USO)","BL-USO"]},{"id":"352148","key":"sof","name":"Scholars of Finance","shortName":"SOF","summary":"A rapidly growing national organization on a mission to solve the world’s largest problems by investing in undergraduate students through leadership development, mentorship, and the active support of hundreds of purpose-driven executives and investors.","description":"Scholars of Finance is a national organization on a mission to inspire character and integrity in the finance leaders of tomorrow.\n\nWe seek to solve the world’s largest problems by investing in undergraduate students through leadership development, mentorship, and the active support of hundreds of purpose-driven finance executives and investors.\n\nWith corporate partners including Goldman Sachs, Black Rock, Piper Sandler, Morgan Stanley, Blackstone, Charles Schwab, and more, our members go on to join top firms, funds, and a life-long support community that empowers them to spend their careers serving the greater good using the biggest lever in the world: finance.\n\nScholars of Finance welcomes new member every semester, the application for the Fall 2026 will be opening soon. Stay tuned for upcoming announcements regarding recruitment.\n\nPlease visit our official website scholarsoffinance.org, and our recruitment slide deck for more information.\n\nNOTE: Clicking join on BeInvolved will not result in admittance to SOF.","categories":["Academic and Professional","International and Multicultural","Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"421893","key":"sigmaetapiiu","name":"Sigma Eta Pi","shortName":"SEP","summary":"A co-ed professional fraternity dedicated not to setting a path for you, but to supporting you on whatever path you carve. Our members are ambitious and goal oriented individuals looking to use the entrepreneurial mindset in their various industries.","description":"A co-ed professional fraternity dedicated not to setting a path for you, but to supporting you on whatever path you carve.\n\nOur mission is to create environments where university students can exercise their creativity, intellect, and problem-solving skills with the support of close-knit community. Nationally, our members have started ventures in every industry from education to technology. Every one of our members has a demonstrable passion for learning, driving change, and self-improvement. \n\nLearn more about recruitment by reaching out to 916-597-7563.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Service and Philanthropy","Z - New Member Training","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133451","key":"seek","name":"Social Engagement and Education at Kelley","shortName":"SEEK","summary":"Social Engagement and Education at Kelley (SEEK) expands the boundaries of business by empowering students to apply their professional and diverse skillsets in exploring the intersection between for-profit enterprise and social responsibility.","description":"As a member of KISI, Social Engagement and Education at Kelley (SEEK) strives to create unique, hands-on experiences that simultaneously give back to the community. We connect future business leaders to socially responsible companies and instill the concept that business can be both profitable and have a positive social impact.\n\nSEEK aims to:\n- Exhibit rewarding ways to give back to the community through non-traditional initiatives \n- Empower students to use their skills to make an impact and gain real-world experience\n- Explore impactful and Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) related career opportunities\n- Collaborate with various companies to help them solve their CSR issues\n\nTo learn more:\n\nOur website: https://sites.google.com/iu.edu/seekatiu/home \n\nOr follow us on Instagram: @seek.iu","categories":["IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133510","key":"sas","name":"Student Accounting Society","shortName":"SAS","summary":"Student Accounting Society is a professional organization in the Kelley School of Business that holds professional, social and community service events. This organization is open to all students, not just Accounting majors.","description":"Welcome to SAS!\n\nThe Student Accounting Society (SAS) is proud to be the top accounting organization at Indiana University that was founded by Ed Kelley himself. With SAS you will have the opportunity to advance your professional and personal skills, in which I would like to invite you to join today!\n\nAt SAS we welcome any and all majors to join, regardless if you are Kelley or not! The goal of SAS is to connect our members with the tools they need to be successful throughout their time in college and beyond. We focus on professional, community service, and social events that each expand your network.\n\nIf you have any questions or concerns regarding the Student Accounting Society or how to join us, please reach out to our officer team through the email listed on this page. For questions specific to a certain aspect of our organization, or for general club information, visit our website. We are excited to see you soon!\n\nBe sure to join our 2025-2026 GroupMe.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"225559","key":"summitimpacttrust","name":"Summit Impact Trust at IU","shortName":null,"summary":"Summit Impact Trust is a mission-driven philanthropic trust that invests ethically to fund high-impact causes like education, healthcare, and climate action—turning financial growth into lasting social good.","description":"Summit Impact Trust is a mission-driven philanthropic trust that reinvents how charitable capital works. Guided by the motto “Invest. Grow. Give.”, the Trust ethically invests its funds to generate returns that are then donated to high-impact causes. With a focus on transparency and measurable outcomes, Summit Impact Trust supports initiatives in women’s protection, children’s healthcare, veteran wellness, housing, climate action, and education. Operating with lean overhead and strong ethical standards, it aims to make philanthropy both sustainable and transformative.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133241","key":"scoma","name":"Supply Chain and Operations Management Association","shortName":"SCOMA","summary":"The Supply Chain and Operations Management Association is a Kelley organization that offers its members numerous opportunities to learn about operations and supply chain management including current event discussions, site tours and corporate speakers.","description":"SCOMA, the Supply Chain and Operations Management Association, is a Kelley organization that offers students a chance to explore Supply Chain Management and Operations Management opportunities. Members are provided opportunities to gain knowledge and insight into the operations of a variety of industries. Site tours are available for students to tour distribution centers, production facilities, and warehouses. SCOMA also strives to provide its members benefits by bringing companies to campus. In the past, we have brought the VP of Retail for Exel, Dan McNutt, as well as professionals from firms such as Coyote Logistics, General Mills, Cummins, and several others. By bringing companies to campus, SCOMA provides its members opportunities to learn and network. It is our mission to provide members as many opportunities as possible to be meet and network with industry professionals. By providing site tours, speakers from companies, and club involvement, SCOMA offers its members numerous opportunities to learn about operations and supply chain management. SCOMA is a growing organization and takes an active approach in member professional development.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"386472","key":"sustainablefinanceiu","name":"Sustainable Finance Club at Indiana University","shortName":null,"summary":"The Sustainable Finance Club at IU exposes students to the role of finance in evolving environmental and social impact. Through real-world cases and industry engagement, members gain the skills to drive responsible, forward-thinking financial strategies.","description":"The Sustainable Finance Club at IU provides students with the opportunity to explore the intersection between finance and sustainability in the professional world. Open to all majors and class years, the club provides hands-on experience and the opportunity to hear from professionals in the sustainable finance world regarding topics such as ESG (environmental, social, and governance) compliance, sustainable investing, sustainability reporting, corporate responsibility, ethical financial decision making, and more. Through research projects, speaker events, and collaborative discussion, members gain a deeper understanding of how financial tools can drive a positive impact in the world around us. \n\n-\n\nBy connecting with industry leaders and examining real world sustainability challenges, students develop the skills necessary to lead in a rapidly evolving financial and environmental landscape. Whether pursuing careers in investment banking, consulting, corporate finance, nonprofit work, or any other financial career, members of the Sustainable Finance Club are equipped with the ability to make responsible, forward-thinking decisions that help shape a more sustainable global economy. \n\n-\n\nHave questions or want to join? Contact us at sustainf@iu.edu or our GroupMe using the link on this page!","categories":["Academic and Professional","Advocacy and Political","Environmental and Sustainability","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133457","key":"tamidatiu","name":"TAMID Group at Indiana University","shortName":"TAMID at IU","summary":"An apolitical, areligious student run organization designed to provide business-minded students with real world international business experience through consulting and investing in Israeli companies.","description":"TAMID Group at IU is a nonprofit organization dedicated to empowering undergraduate students by developing their professional skills through hands-on experiences in business and entrepreneurship. Our program begins with a semester-long comprehensive education curriculum, allowing students to choose between Consulting or Finance Education.\n\nFollowing this, students engage in real-world consulting projects, manage investment funds, and have the opportunity to gain practical experience through internships in Israel, the startup nation. TAMID provides a dynamic platform for students to apply classroom knowledge to real-world scenarios, fostering a deep understanding of the business landscape and equipping them with the skills necessary for successful careers.\n\nOur application is on our website at IUTAMID.COM \n\nYou can also apply here - https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf8qL-i9fu9oiM7wQeU52dgz243fpqskPYeOv2XPKmrvPrChw/viewform","categories":["Academic and Professional","International and Multicultural","Social","Service and Philanthropy","Z - Travel - International","Z - New Member Training","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Government, International Affairs, + Public Policy","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"134452","key":"tmc","name":"Technology Management Club","shortName":"TMC","summary":"TMC is a student-led organization connecting students interested in technology and business. We explore current tech trends and help members build industry-relevant skills through workshops, networking events, and professional development opportunities.","description":"The Technology Management Club (TMC) at Indiana University is the Kelley School of Business’s leading organization for students passionate about technology and its role in shaping modern business. Our mission is to explore emerging tech trends, cultivate leadership skills, and help members grow professionally in tech-driven industries.\n\nWe achieve this through a diverse range of activities including:\n\n• Guest speaker events featuring industry professionals\n\n• Networking sessions with peers, alumni, and employers\n\n• Interactive workshops and learning seminars\n\n• Community service projects and outreach\n\n• Leadership development opportunities\n\n• Tech-focused social events\n\nTMC is open to students of all majors and experience levels who are curious about the intersection of business and technology. Our membership continues to grow each semester as we build a supportive, innovative, and collaborative community.\n\nIf you\u0027re interested in joining TMC, please request membership through BeInvolved and join the GroupMe (link is located in our instagram bio) to receive updates. \n\nFollow our Instagram (@tmc.iu) to stay further updated on our current events!\n\nContact tmcindianauniversity@gmail.com if you gave any questions","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133430","key":"adclubiu","name":"The Ad Club at Indiana University","shortName":"Ad Club @ IU","summary":"You have the drive. We have the direction.","description":"The Ad Club at Indiana University strives to convey industry trends, create meaningful portfolio work, and connect members with peers, professors and professionals. We aim to prepare driven students for the dynamic advertising ecosystem by\r\n directing them to relevant opportunities and available resources.\n\nWe do it all in Ad Club and we’re always open to trying new ideas — who knows? Maybe you’ll have our next one.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","IU Kelley School of Business","IU Media School","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"134357","key":"businessedge","name":"The Business Edge","shortName":"TBE","summary":"The Business Edge is committed to developing talented students into successful business professionals.","description":"The Business Edge is committed to developing talented students into successful business professionals.\n\njoin the slack https://join.slack.com/t/thebusinessedge/shared_invite/zt-47b5y37yf-rqV7UnLQYnNh9uILdeI8Kw","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"421224","key":"thebusinessnetwork","name":"The Business Network","shortName":"TBN","summary":"The Business Network (TBN) empowers students to master networking as a foundation of success. We build authentic relationship skills that open opportunities across business—emphasizing confidence, curiosity, and lasting connections.","description":"The Business Network is a student-led IU organization that redefines what it means to prepare for a career in business. Instead of making networking a side topic, TBN places it at the core of our curriculum. Through a structured semester-long program, members learn how to initiate and sustain meaningful professional relationships across all related business fields including finance, consulting, marketing, and etc. \n\nTBN hosts networking simulations, interactive workshops, and guest speaker events that allow students to practice real-world interactions in a supportive environment where mistakes become learning opportunities. The club also maintains a shared contact and alumni database to help members sustain relationships and expand their professional reach long after graduation.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"149121","key":"bwos","name":"The Business World of Sports Club","shortName":"BWOS","summary":"The Business World of Sports Club is designed to equip students with the skills necessary to be successful in the business side of the sports industry. Through several interactive events, students will gain hands-on experience in the sports world.","description":"FOLLOW OUR INSTAGRAM @bwosiu TO STAY UP TO DATE! The Business World of Sports Club is designed to equip students with the skills necessary to be successful in the business side of the sports industry. Members will attend meetings and events throughout the school year that will help them establish networking connections to help secure career opportunities. Throughout the school year, The Business World of Sports Club will host guest speakers, hold case competitions, professional development series, and many other great opportunities. Members will be able to apply their knowledge from their business courses to real-world sports scenarios.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","Sports and Recreation","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Career Community - Marketing, Advertising, + Public Relations","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"139215","key":"twn","name":"The Women\u0027s Network","shortName":"TWN ","summary":"The Women’s Network is an all-inclusive Kelley School of Business undergraduate organization dedicated to supporting and advancing the careers and future education of undergraduate women within Indiana University.","description":"The Women’s Network is an all-inclusive undergraduate organization dedicated to supporting and advancing the careers and future education of undergraduate women within Indiana University.\n\nThe main objectives of the organization are to provide the undergraduate women of Indiana University with a network of peers, faculty, staff and corporate and alumni women to offer communal support and inspiration, as well as meet the professional development needs of any woman regardless of major.\n\nFormed in October 2015, The Women’s Network is partly modeled off of the Forté Foundation curriculum intended to, “launch women into fulfilling, significant careers through access to business education, opportunities, and a community of successful women.” (Forte Foundation) Our organization can be joined through the following link: https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/organization/TWN (on this page click the button \"Join Organization\" and you will be included in all future emailing lists.)","categories":["Social","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Career Community - Marketing, Advertising, + Public Relations","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"393678","key":"thriveatiu","name":"Thrive Solutions Club at IU","shortName":"Thrive","summary":"This is a biweekly commitment that students from any major can join. The purpose of the club is to help small businesses and give students the chance to hear about real problems companies face. We brainstorm ideas to help small businesses.","description":"We started this club with the hopes of helping small businesses and nonprofits while helping students learn about real challenges real companies face. During the meeting we will have a 15 minute presentation informing students on the business and its challenges. Then we will break off into groups to discuss and come up with creative solutions for the business. Then, the exec team will email these solutions to the business to help them thrive! This is great to help students learn how to face challenges in a business and hopefully our ideas can help out the business.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133493","key":"toastmastersatksb","name":"Toastmasters at the Kelley School of Business","shortName":"Toastmasters at KSB","summary":"Toastmasters is a public speaking organization that allows students to practice different types of public speaking in a laid-back setting. It\u0027s the Indiana University chapter of Toastmasters International.","description":"Toastmasters at the Kelley School of Business is IU\u0027s own student run chapter of Toastmasters International. This organization has grown to become a world leader in helping people become more competent and comfortable in front of an audience. It now has over 350,000 members in nearly 17,000 clubs in 143 countries, offering a proven, and enjoyable, way to improve communication and leadership skills.\n\nKSB Toastmasters meets Tuesdays from 8:00 - 9:00pm in Hodge Hall! Further announcements like room number and time-sensitive information will be provided in the GroupMe.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Arts and Entertainment","Graduate","International and Multicultural","Social","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Visual, Written, + Performing Arts","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133249","key":"trockmaniu","name":"Trockman Microfinance Initiative","shortName":"Trockman","summary":"Trockman Microfinance Initiative (TMI) at IU aims to explore the greater microfinance sector through global nonprofit and NGO consulting.","description":"Trockman Microfinance Initiative (TMI) at Indiana University Bloomington (IU) is a student organization that is part of the Kelley Institute for Social Impact (KISI). Our mission is poverty alleviation through business.\n\nIn order to accomplish this, the main strategy we focus on is microfinance consulting, both in the United States and overseas. We work in teams to consult with nonprofits, travel internationally, host speaker events, hold weekly discussions and more. Ultimately, we make use of concepts from the Kelley School of Business curriculum to improve the well-being of others on both a local and global scale.\n\nFrom educational events to volunteering in the community to consulting with local nonprofits, Trockman puts on and participates in a number of ongoing projects, activities, and events. Our organization conducts research, hosts panel discussions, sponsors fundraisers, and consults with nonprofit organizations.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Service and Philanthropy","Z - Travel","Z - Travel - International","Z - Travel - Service","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133416","key":"ubdc","name":"Undergraduate Business Diversity Council","shortName":"UBDC","summary":"The Undergraduate Business Diversity Council is an organization committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive environment where students can develop as business leaders alongside people from distinct backgrounds.","description":"Applications open at the beginning of each semester. Follow our instagram learn more about our organization and/or apply to be a member. \n\nOur Mission: The Undergraduate Business Diversity Council develops future leaders in the ever-evolving business world. We strive to produce talent that excels in a dynamic, diverse work environment to create positive change for the future. In our organization, we work to not only grow and develop our members as professionals but also connect students to top companies in the field of business.","categories":["Advocacy and Political","International and Multicultural","Social","Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"147399","key":"urt","name":"Undergraduate Research and Trading","shortName":"URT","summary":"Successful trading requires quantifiable and consistent edge. We emphasize the incorporation of financial derivatives into trade ideas driven by fundamental alpha models and statistical arbitrage. Learn how to trade options with free paper money accounts.","description":"URT is the sole club at IU that teaches options trading. Our organization strives to teach those who are eager to learn about how to not only trade but also strategize and think originally. We also cover all aspects of the financial\r\n markets that are necessary for you to have a general understanding of the industry, including career options, equities, fixed income, and futures. Our primary goal is to expose members to various Options trading techniques and give them the opportunity to\r\n test these strategies in the real world through a simulated platform. \n\nStrategic Trading will potentially help those who have an interest in personal trading or plan to pursue proprietary trading as a career. The leaders in trading are the ones who will profit.\n\nWe do not invest money or trade as an organization, but you may do so personally at your own evaluation and risk. \n\nJoin the Group Me for meeting information: \r\nhttps://groupme.com/join_group/58346843/M4RyvO6o","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"405761","key":"vic","name":"Value Investing Club","shortName":"VIC","summary":"The club will foster a community of students passionate about long-term, fundamental investing strategies. We explore topics such as intrinsic value, DCF valuations, and will feature presentations on investors such as Warren Buffett and Peter Lynch.","description":"The Value Investing Club is dedicated to teaching an elevated understanding of value investing principles among students who are passionate about finance and investing. Our mission is to provide a platform for students to learn, engage, and apply the timeless principles of value investing, inspired by the approaches of investment titans like Benjamin Graham and Warren Buffett. Through a combination of presentations, guest speakers, and hands-on application, members will gain exposure to fundamental analysis, portfolio management, and market valuation techniques. We conduct regular meetings that feature stock pitches, financial statement analysis sessions, and interactive discussions on investment opportunities and market trends. Our club emphasizes critical thinking and a long-term mindset as key values, thereby fostering an analytical mindset essential for discovering undervalued securities (or other assets) in the market. We are genuinely committed to helping members expand their knowledge and build practical skills through networking events, mentorship from finance professionals, and access to exclusive resources and tools. Members of the club will enhance their financial knowledge and develop lasting relationships within a community that shares a passion for value-driven investment strategies and long-term growth.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"304965","key":"wealthstrategyassociation","name":"Wealth Strategy Association","shortName":"WSA","summary":"WSA examines ways to build wealth through guest speakers and workshops. With a focus on passive income and entrepreneurship, the WSA exposes students to many different areas of wealth and managing their own financials.","description":"The Wealth Strategy Association (WSA) aims to educate, inform and collaborate with students at Indiana University about the multitude of methods to build passive income and manage wealth. The term \"passive income\" refers to income earned from venture activities that require minimal and little-to-no ongoing effort.\n\nPassive income can be divided into two fundamental forms:\n\n1. Entrepreneurial (e.g. affiliate marketing, app development and content creation)\n\n2. Financial (e.g. dividend investing, real estate and fixed income)\n\nTo begin earning passive income, you need to be financially literate, with an open mind and eagerness to learn. While money doesn\u0027t grow on trees, when your streams of passive income are developed, not only are they expendable, but the streams have money-making potential to last a lifetime if you can manage your wealth well. Though this might be your first time getting involved with passive income, once you understand how to get started, you can discover and enjoy a healthy financial future.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"145263","key":"womenandcompany","name":"Women \u0026 Co.","shortName":"WoCo","summary":"Women \u0026 Co.’s purpose is to bring together a group of like-minded women, who are knowledgeable, well rounded, and driven. The Co is more than company.","description":"Women \u0026 Co.\u0027s objective is to bring together a group of like-minded women, who are knowledgeable, well-rounded and driven. The organization name represents all that it encompasses. \n\nThe Co is more than company.\n\nconversation | commitment | cognizance | comprehension | cosmopolitan | consciousness | counter points | coaching | coalition | conduit | coexistence\n\nWomen \u0026 Co. is a platform for women in business to engage, educate, and empower each other. Women \u0026 Co. engages in networking events and professional development workshops. Alongside working with our members, Women \u0026 Co’s mission is to educate and work with the IU community as a whole as members engage in networking events and professional development workshops. Further, the organization works with the IU community to educate students on how women can be successful throughout their personal and professional careers. Women \u0026 Co. plans events focused on open dialogue and communication to empower one another and develop personally.\n\nWomen \u0026 Co. is a growing organization that pushes its members to broaden their horizons. We strive to create a community of strong women through engaging, educating and empowering our members.  \n\nCo is more than Company.\n\nWomen \u0026 Co. is composed of six integral teams each having a Chief Officer who oversees and guides committees towards their goals. The Executive Board consists of the President, Vice President, Chief Financial Officer, Co-Chief Officers of Recruitment, and 8 Chief Officers. The eight core teams are based off of the most prominent departments in the business industry: Human Resources, DEI, Corporate Relations, Finance, Philanthropy, Marketing, Professional Development, and Alumni Relations.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"419217","key":"wise","name":"Women Impacting Supply Chain Excellence at Indiana University","shortName":"WISE at Indiana University","summary":"The mission of WISE is to empower students interested in studying or pursuing a career in supply chain management through networking, personal and professional development, leadership skills, and industry knowledge.","description":"WISE at IU is a student organization aimed at attracting and empowering female students pursuing careers in supply chain\nmanagement. The organization focuses on networking, personal and professional development, leadership skills, and industry\nknowledge to prepare members for success in the field. Our chapter provides a platform for students to connect, learn and grow\ntogether.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"181871","key":"wia","name":"Women in Accounting","shortName":"WIA","summary":"We aim to provide members with the proper tools for life post-graduation by helping develop them professionally, expand their network, and connect with others who also have an interest in business, specifically accounting.","description":"Women in Accounting is a student-led organization dedicated to empowering women in the accounting field through professional development, corporate engagement, and social connections. Our three types of meetings—Professional Development, Corporate, and Social—help\r\n members strengthen essential skills like resume writing and mock interviews, expand their professional networks through corporate events, and build lasting connections with peers. Whether you\u0027re looking to refine your career skills, meet industry professionals,\r\n or connect with like-minded students, Women in Accounting provides the support and resources to help you succeed.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Graduate","Social","Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Career Community - Marketing, Advertising, + Public Relations","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133312","key":"wib","name":"Women in Business","shortName":"WiB","summary":"Women in Business (WiB) is an undergraduate organization dedicated to developing members personally and professionally. We share similar goals, values, and visions, yet have unique personal backgrounds and experiences.","description":"Women in Business (WiB) is an undergraduate organization dedicated to developing members personally and professionally. We share similar goals, values, and visions, yet have unique personal backgrounds and experiences. We form\r\n new relationships that help us set and achieve goals, both in and out of the classroom. WiB benefits its members in different ways, whether it be developing professional skills, finding a community on campus, or achieving personal growth.\n\nTo learn more about the membership process, please visit our website \r\nhere. Recruitment is open to all Freshmen and Sophomores each Fall.","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"238016","key":"wibt","name":"Women in Business Technology at IU","shortName":"WiBT","summary":"Women in Business Technology is dedicated to building a vibrant community of women who are passionate about the intersection of business and technology, and eager to develop the skills needed to thrive and lead in this dynamic field.","description":"Women in Business Technology (WiBT) is a dynamic and inclusive community dedicated to empowering women interested in the intersection of business and technology. Our mission is to create a supportive environment where women can explore technology-focused\r\n studies, develop essential skills for their careers, and connect with peers and professionals in the field.\n\nIn alignment with Indiana University’s commitment to fostering innovation and inclusion, WiBT provides members with opportunities to grow through educational programs, professional networking, and community-focused initiatives. From job shadows, site visits,\r\n and speaking panels to exclusive networking events, WiBT equips members with the tools and connections needed to thrive in a traditionally male-dominated industry.\n\nLooking ahead, WiBT aims to give back to the community by championing causes related to women and technology, furthering our commitment to meaningful impact.Whether you are pursuing a tech-focused major, developing your skills, or exploring new interests,\r\n WiBT is your platform to learn, connect, and achieve your goals in business and technology. Join us and be part of a community dedicated to empowering women and shaping the future!\n\nPlease join our Groupme or follow us on\n\nInstagram for more regular updates!","categories":["Advocacy and Political","Service and Philanthropy","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Career Community - Technology, Data, + Analytics","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"393076","key":"wims","name":"Women in Marketing \u0026 Sales","shortName":"WiMS","summary":"WiMS develops confident women leaders in marketing and sales by fostering initiative, curiosity, integrity, networking, and sisterhood. We empower members to grow professionally, build lasting connections, and create meaningful impact in business.","description":"Welcome to Women in Marketing \u0026 Sales (WiMS), where ambition meets innovation and women empower one another to redefine the future of business. More than a student organization, WiMS is a community of driven women who are passionate about developing as leaders, building meaningful connections, and creating lasting impact in marketing, sales, and beyond.\n\nAt the heart of WiMS are our core values of initiative, sisterhood, curiosity, integrity, and networking. We encourage women to take initiative in pursuing their goals, embrace new opportunities, and lead with confidence. Through sisterhood, we foster a supportive environment where women uplift one another, celebrate each other\u0027s successes, and build lifelong friendships. Curiosity drives our commitment to continuous learning, professional growth, and exploration of new ideas and industries. Integrity guides our actions and interactions, helping members develop into ethical and trustworthy leaders. Through networking, we connect women with peers, alumni, and industry professionals who inspire growth and open doors to future opportunities.\n\nWiMS provides members with access to professional development workshops, guest speakers, mentorship opportunities, company visits, networking events, and leadership experiences designed to prepare women for successful careers. Whether members are exploring career paths, seeking internships, building professional skills, or preparing for life after graduation, WiMS offers the resources and community needed to succeed.\n\nIn our community, bold ideas are encouraged, friendships are forged, and every woman is valued for the unique perspective she brings. Together, we are cultivating the next generation of women leaders who will drive innovation, challenge expectations, and shape the future of business with confidence, purpose, and impact.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"134354","key":"waconsulting","name":"Women\u0027s Association for Consulting","shortName":"WAC","summary":"WAC empowers women to break into consulting through workshops, speaker events, and mentorship. Join our supportive community to gain skills, build your network, and grow into the confident leader you’re meant to be.","description":"Women’s Association for Consulting (WAC) is an empowering, student-led organization committed to helping women break into the world of consulting with confidence, community, and clarity. Founded at Indiana University, WAC offers\r\n a collaborative space for aspiring consultants to build technical knowledge, expand industry networks, and develop leadership skills in a supportive environment.\n\nOur club bridges the gap between ambition and access by providing curated programming—from speaker events with top-tier consulting firms and interactive case prep workshops to peer mentorship and networking opportunities. WAC’s executive board is\r\n structured to ensure members receive holistic support across personal, professional, and academic goals. Whether you\u0027re exploring the industry for the first time or preparing for a competitive internship, WAC is here to help you take the next step with purpose.\n\nWe believe in championing and redefining what it means to be a woman in consulting, and building a community where ambition is met with actionable guidance. Join WAC and become part of a driven, inclusive network paving the way for the next generation\r\n of leaders in consulting.","categories":["Academic and Professional","Social","IU Kelley School of Business","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]},{"id":"133476","key":"wfa","name":"Women\u0027s Financial Association","shortName":"WFA","summary":"The mission of WFA is to assist its members in graduating with a better understanding of the finance industry and with a network of peers who will support each individual in her quest to reach her goals.","description":"Women’s Financial Association is an organization dedicated to promoting the success of women with a passion for finance at Indiana University Bloomington. Our mission is to assist our members in graduating with a better understanding of the finance industry and with a network of peers and mentors who will support each individual in her quest to reach her goals.  \n\nWe believe that formally organizing a network of female finance students and alumni will not only enhance the education of the Kelley School of Business’ female finance students, but will also make Kelley’s Finance Department the premier recruiting grounds for companies in search of first-class female finance students.\n\nFor more information, visit our website or email kelley.wfa@outlook.com","categories":["Academic and Professional","IU Kelley School of Business","Career Community - Finance, Consulting, Management, + Sales","Self Governed Student Organization (SGSO)","BL-SGSO"]}];
